"id": "passive-present",
"el": "Παθητικά ρήματα Ι: -ομαι, -άμαι, -ιέμαι, -ούμαι",
"title": "Passive and middle verbs I: present and imperfect",
"span": "A2–B1",
"blurb": "The verbs ending in -μαι: their four present patterns (έρχομαι, θυμάμαι, στενοχωριέμαι, ασχολούμαι), the imperfect in -όμουν, and the four things -μαι can mean: passive, reflexive, reciprocal, or just an ordinary verb (deponent).",
"intro": [
{
"p": "Every Greek verb ending in **-μαι** uses the \"passive\" set of endings. But not all of them are passive in meaning. **Έρχομαι** \"I come\", **σκέφτομαι** \"I think\", **κοιμάμαι** \"I sleep\" are perfectly ordinary verbs that simply have these endings. Many very common verbs belong here, so the endings are a must from A2 on."
},
